The deployed Vercel bundle was baking in an old preview hostname
(belong-together.preview.emergentagent.com) that now returns 404. Any
client-side admin API call — including /api/cms/auth/login — was hitting
a dead URL, which is why signing in to Mission Control failed.

Fix:
- next.config.js: update the NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL default to the live
  pod hostname (friendplace-v1.preview.emergentagent.com).
- New lib/api-base.ts: single source of truth for the backend URL with
  the hardcoded fallback baked into the client bundle at build time.
- lib/cms-api.ts + lib/api.ts now import API_BASE from api-base.
- All remaining admin/public callers replace their "|| ''" with the
  same explicit fallback so no future build regression can silently
  route requests to the Vercel domain again.

No env vars, secrets, robots settings, DNS, or Vercel project config
changed. FRIENDPLACE_INDEXABLE behaviour is untouched — the site
stays hidden from search engines. Mobile app (/app/frontend and
/app/backend) is completely untouched. Post-login redirect route
(/admin/dashboard) is unchanged.

Verified locally: production build compiles clean, login flow
succeeds end-to-end (POST /api/cms/auth/login returns 200, redirect
to /admin/dashboard renders Mission Control).
